Now these two are a TOUGH combo to do.  Atheist is annoying, but once you 
find expensive water, you can deal with it. The lack of BUC and nifty prayer 
effects are a bit sad, but it's doable.  Illiterate is just as hard: no 
e-word, no scrolls, no spells, gotta remember to engrave x any time you're 
going to test a wand... Yadda yadda yadda.

Doing both is a serious pain.  But the wishes I got made it bearable.

On level 2 a wand offers a wish when I go to make an x.  I decide to take a 
chance, i'm level 3 and 25 hps.  I wish for the blessed PYEC.  The blasting 
takes me to 3 hps.  I then zap again and try for a +3 SDSM... darn, +0.  Zap 
again... ok, give me the +3 Grayswandir.   I wonder the dungeon working on 
my saber skill.  On level 3 I find a large liquor store, two different 
expensive clear potions, and some probable !oGA or GL.  On level 4 is the 
minestair and a chest in the down staircase room that I make my stash.  I 
stash the whip and jacket for later.  The mines are lit so I go down.  I 
find a kickable gray stone, touchstone tells me it's a luckstone, yay! 
Minetown is spooky, no shopkeepers other than the lighting shop.  It's not a 
boneslevel either... what are the odds of that?  Itzchak has two expensive 
lamps, but only 4 candles.  Gotta remember to save a wish for those.  Oh, 
and the temple is co-aligned.  Arrgh!

Back up, head down DL 6 has a throne room, no ID.  I go past the oracle and 
do Sokoban.  I get the bag, and toss the gray unicorn in the zoo some gems 
to max my luck.  It's good to have a touchstone.  Level 11 is a bonesfile 
Bigroom, the bones of an S with a dog named rusty.  He went on a rubber 
chicken rampage, but didn't survive.  I never picked up his Excalibur, but 
took his GDSM, (it's +3) and his magic lamp and wand collection.  Level 15 
is the rogue level and 16 has the quest portal.  I move on (clevel 11)  I 
head back to do minesend, maybe I'll get lucky and hit the winecellar.  Not 
this time.  Of course it's the haunted library... no biggie, the vampires 
don't like grayswandir and I get a spare luckstone.  I bless them both after 
washing out my most numerous potion.  I have no idea what I washed out, 
probably healing.  I needed the water at that point.  I also bless the bag 
so I can unburden myself and still carry my wand collection.  I've engrave 
id'ed wishing, enlightenment, digging, fire and cold by now.  I zap id 
teleportation after getting the vanishing message message.  I head on down 
and on level 20 I find another WoW on the deck.  I use the PYEC to recharge 
the first one and replace my +2 elven cloak with a +3 oilskin cloak. I then 
go to wrest and discover that the PYEC does blessed recharge WoW's.  Is this 
a bug?  Either way I get +0 speed boots and a +3 t-shirt.  I waste two more 
wishes trying to get +3 speed boots. (wrested from first wand and first wish 
from second)  I then decide to toss the leather gloves and get GoP.

Level 23 is medusa, I freeze my way across and beat medusa while blinded. 
As an arch I decide not to break the statues.  I tin medusa, starting a tin 
collection.  Two maze levels come between medusa and the castle. At the 
castle I freeze one square of the moat and then use a /oStriking to take out 
the drawbridge from a safe distance.  I wait in the corridor from the left 
side maze and fight the soldiers etc. from there.  I advance out to grab a 
wand of death at one point.  (The soldier only used two charges before 
closing on me)

After clearing the castle I grab the WoW and re-charge my second wand with 
the PYEC.  I head back to the quest (hit level 14 clearing the barracks) 
with all +3 gear and two empty wands (one that can be re-charged)  I decided 
to go with the [SoR, forgoing more offense for a better AC.

The quest isn't hard, I get the orb without killing the Minion, then hunt 
him down for the bell.  I keep the orb stashed for the ascension run.

The VS is on l48, time to get the must-read book of the dungeon.  Rodney 
double troubled as soon as I opened his tower, but a rubber chicken leaves 
two statues (on the same square) and me with that book.  I wish up the 
candles and the ritual goes well, I dump the invocation artifacts.  I head 
down, killing one master lich and as I'm cutting a path through the 
graveyard there's a pretty yellow c.  That corpse left a LOT of statues in 
the sanctum, including the high priest. I've managed to sock away 4 !oGL, so 
I curse them and start my way up. I use them in the sanctum, Orcustown, Baal 
and Asmo.  The mysterious force means I had to walk Baal and Asmo as well. 
The run up from the castle is uneventful, I pick up my starting gear and 
head for the planes.  The Orb only failed once (on water) luckily it had 5 
charges.  With 300 hps I did ok on air, played avoidance on fire.  The 
portals on Fire and Earth were near the middle of the map, with the Air and 
water ones at the far side.  Astral required a full tour, as I kept making 
bad decisions.  I nailed famine with one of my /oDeath, but his altar 
(center) was lawful,  went to death next but that was(I burned my first "oLS 
here) Chaotic (right) Finally, after fighting my way back, and burning a 
second "oLS, I got to the left hand altar and whistled in my guardian angel.

Other than the ghost town minetown, I also ran into 2 player monsters in the 
valley (strange) and 4 on the astral (scary) only one had an artifact, Fire 
Brand.  And how about the 4 magic markers for a joke by the RNG?

